   panel clipped itself at 50% of ITSELF — with a caption sharing the band those
   are different lines, and the lit horizon crossed the panel two-thirds down
   while the clip stayed at the middle. Now one `--seam` on `.split` drives the
   clip of BOTH copies, the full-bleed background's hard stop, the lit rule and
   its printed echo, so they cannot drift at any viewport size. The breathing
   room above and below comes from the NEIGHBOURS (a dark sky above, a paper
   block below), never from padding inside the split. */
.v7 .seam { position: relative; }
